\[
\operatorname{proj}_{\mathbf{w}} \mathbf{v} = \frac{\mathbf{v} \cdot \mathbf{w}}{\mathbf{w} \cdot \mathbf{w}} \mathbf{w}
\]
If we multiply $\mathbf{v}$ by a scalar $k$, then the projection of $k\mathbf{v}$ onto $\mathbf{w}$ is:
\[
\operatorname{proj}_{\mathbf{w}} (k \mathbf{v}) = \frac{(k \mathbf{v}) \cdot \mathbf{w}}{\mathbf{w} \cdot \mathbf{w}} \mathbf{w} = k \frac{\mathbf{v} \cdot \mathbf{w}}{\mathbf{w} \cdot \mathbf{w}} \mathbf{w} = k \operatorname{proj}_{\mathbf{w}} \mathbf{v}
\]
So if $\operatorname{proj}_{\mathbf{w}} \mathbf{v} = \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 0 \\ -3 \end{pmatrix}$, then
\[
\operatorname{proj}_{\mathbf{w}} (-2 \mathbf{v}) = -2 \operatorname{proj}_{\mathbf{w}} \mathbf{v} = -2 \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 0 \\ -3 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} -2 \\ 0 \\ 6 \end{pmatrix}
\]
